#   draft-newer        the served draft says what the page says and the pinned data (tools/css/WEBREF_COMMIT) predates it
#   wpt-tentative      the page is a tentative test: no specification decides it yet
#   needs-environment  the answer depends on the document, the layout or the user agent, which a parser does not have
#   wpt-wrong          the page contradicts the served draft
#   served-text        a quoted sentence of the served text, read alone, entails the library's answer and not the page's; the reason ends in [record: *] (or [record: <case id>; ...]),
#                      the recorded answers of both pinned browsers (tools/conformance/css_browser_answers.jsonl), which the gate looks up and refuses when absent
#   browsers-differ    the served text is silent and the two pinned browsers answer differently (the gate checks that they do): the value is kept as written
